{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration/recovery policy in specifications. The policy gives one controllable action per decision/recovery state, keeps all states total on uncontrollable sensor events, prefers forward progress in clear space, uses short directed turns for side/front obstacles, uses move_backward only in a dedicated front-recovery branch, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated last-resort stuck state after repeated front blockage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensor outcomes from motion capability in G so E can impose a deterministic supervisor policy cleanly",
    "Use decision and one-shot commit/recovery states in E: forward in clear, clockwise for left obstacle, counterclockwise for right obstacle, brief backward only after repeated front blockage, and full_rotate only from a dedicated last-resort state"
  ],
